  "answer": "This is a storefront discount bug. I\u2019ll follow the bug-fix playbook, reproduce the dated special-price path, and fix the cause.The admin mapper stores the special end date in the start-date field, and the price calculator then rejects a window that has both dates. I\u2019ll lock that in with a failing test before changing either path.A special price with an end date never reached the storefront because the admin product mapper saved that end date into the start-date field, and the price calculator then required the start date to be both before and after today before it would apply a discount. Laziness Protocol kept the change to those two assignments. Fix Root Causes is why both were corrected, since either one alone still hid the discount. Test Behavior Not Implementation and Prove It Works are the new unit tests, which failed on the dated specials and then passed.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am test -Dtest=ProductPriceUtilsSpecialPriceTest,PersistableProductAvailabilityMapperTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"a live admin REST create followed by a storefront product read\", \"products already saved with the end date stored in the start-date column\"], \"missing\": [\"a documented HTTP fixture that creates a product with a dated special and reads the storefront price\"]}",
